@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s48-area-order`
IMPORT `ito-s48a-foreign-worker-regs`
IMPORT `ito-il28-routing`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-28 independent tests (fid-il-28, IL-56). Every expected value is from DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (sha256 93c38b1f...),
-- written from the Hebrew before this encoding was opened. Case ids (A01, C03, ...) are DECIDED-ANSWERS ids.
-- The readings used: `my readings` = F1 declined (AMB-1), F2 A, F4 A (AMB-7), FW1 A (reg 3 gives points without the
-- cited sections' residence conditions), FW2 A, FW3 A, OV declined (AMB-3).
-- Expected failures and refusals are declared in check.sh's expected_failed and named beside each line below.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Independent tests — row IL-28`

§§ `Builders and readings`

`my readings` MEANS `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
    `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `declined where residence decides section 36A`
    `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 for every individual`
    `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `one residence status for the whole tax year`
    `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
    `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
    `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives`
    `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

`my readings with F1 A` MEANS `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
    `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A has no residence condition`
    `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 for every individual`
    `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `one residence status for the whole tax year`
    `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
    `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
    `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives`
    `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

`my readings with F1 B` MEANS `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
    `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
    `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 for every individual`
    `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `one residence status for the whole tax year`
    `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
    `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014`
    `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives`
    `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

-- An Area resident, not an Israeli citizen. fav = s 37 favoured individual, dep = livelihood on him, prf = proved.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      fav IS A BOOLEAN
      dep IS A BOOLEAN
      prf IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`area person` y `woman` w `favoured` fav `dependent` dep `proved` prf MEANS Taxpayer WITH
    `the tax year`                                            IS y
    `an individual`                                           IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                                 IS w
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                     IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area`                                  IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`            IS FALSE
    `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`           IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year`  IS `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
    `a favoured individual within section 37`                 IS fav
    `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`           IS dep
    `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`   IS prf
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS TRUE
    `a worker`                                                IS FALSE
    `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`     IS FALSE
    `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS FALSE
    `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS FALSE
    `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`               IS FALSE
    `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`           IS FALSE
    `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`             IS FALSE
    `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS FALSE
    `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area`  IS 12
    `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`    IS TRUE

-- Area-resident variants of the plain person: citizen, Law of Return, company, Israeli resident, part-year months (0 = whole year).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      cit IS A BOOLEAN
      lor IS A BOOLEAN
      ind IS A BOOLEAN
      isr IS A BOOLEAN
      mo IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`area variant` y `citizen` cit `lawofreturn` lor `individual` ind `israeli` isr `months` mo MEANS Taxpayer WITH
    `the tax year`                                            IS y
    `an individual`                                           IS ind
    `a woman`                                                 IS FALSE
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                     IS isr
    `a resident of the Area`                                  IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`            IS cit
    `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`           IS lor
    `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year`  IS
        IF mo EQUALS 0 THEN `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
        ELSE `a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year` WITH
            `the months of the tax year in which the taxpayer was a resident of the Area` IS mo
    `a favoured individual within section 37`                 IS FALSE
    `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`           IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`   IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS TRUE
    `a worker`                                                IS FALSE
    `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`     IS FALSE
    `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS FALSE
    `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS FALSE
    `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`               IS FALSE
    `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`           IS FALSE
    `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`             IS FALSE
    `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS FALSE
    `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area`  IS 12
    `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`    IS TRUE

-- A foreign worker. lawful = stay and employment permitted; exp = expert/lecturer; b1; car = caring permit; ext = 3A(b) extension;
-- inc = income under 2(1)/(2); isr = Israeli resident for tax; mo = months in Israel or the Area; visa = holds or needs an s 2 visa;
-- area = also a resident of the Area.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      mo IS A NUMBER
      lawful IS A BOOLEAN
      exp IS A BOOLEAN
      b1 IS A BOOLEAN
      car IS A BOOLEAN
      ext IS A BOOLEAN
      inc IS A BOOLEAN
      isr IS A BOOLEAN
      visa IS A BOOLEAN
      area IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`foreign worker` y `woman` w `months` mo `lawfully` lawful `expert` exp `btype` b1 `caring` car `extended` ext `income` inc `israeli` isr `visaneed` visa `arearesident` area MEANS Taxpayer WITH
    `the tax year`                                            IS y
    `an individual`                                           IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                                 IS w
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                     IS isr
    `a resident of the Area`                                  IS area
    `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`            IS FALSE
    `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`           IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year`  IS `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
    `a favoured individual within section 37`                 IS TRUE
    `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`           IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`   IS TRUE
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS TRUE
    `a worker`                                                IS TRUE
    `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`     IS FALSE
    `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS visa
    `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS lawful
    `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`               IS exp
    `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`           IS b1
    `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`             IS car
    `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS ext
    `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area`  IS mo
    `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`    IS inc

-- shorthand: legal caring / legal other / ordinary
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      mo IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`caring worker` y `woman` w `months` mo MEANS `foreign worker` y `woman` w `months` mo `lawfully` TRUE `expert` FALSE `btype` TRUE `caring` TRUE `extended` TRUE `income` TRUE `israeli` FALSE `visaneed` TRUE `arearesident` FALSE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      mo IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`other legal worker` y `woman` w `months` mo MEANS `foreign worker` y `woman` w `months` mo `lawfully` TRUE `expert` FALSE `btype` TRUE `caring` FALSE `extended` FALSE `income` TRUE `israeli` FALSE `visaneed` TRUE `arearesident` FALSE

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total` t `under` r MEANS `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
      v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`money` t `under` r `at` v MEANS `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r `, at` v

